406 0 obj
<<
/Title (Our argument aims to make clear how imperative Jeffery Epstein's social network was in his ability to break the law, forge the truth, and avoid legal repercussions until his arrest in 2019. Epstein surrounded himself with patrons of every profession to create a network in which he had power and influence over those in law enforcement, legal teams, financial power, and many other realms.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 363 0 R
/Next 407 0 R
>>
endobj
407 0 obj
<<
/Title (Epstein was a master at not only recruiting people to his network but, more interestingly, keeping them in. Again, we do not aim to accuse patrons of wrongdoing simply by association, rather to study how their support and relations with Epstein allowed him to create a wall of protection no matter the wrongdoing.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 363 0 R
/Prev 406 0 R
>>
endobj
408 0 obj
<<
/Title (When deciding how we wanted to collect our data, we knew simply sifting through every published document from the Epstein Files trying to find all the email logs would take too much time. Instead, we relied on this website called Jmail for our data collection.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 364 0 R
/Next 439 0 R
>>
endobj
